# Frontend conventions

Full reference: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Skill: [.cursor/skills/react/SKILL.md](../skills/react/SKILL.md).

## Structure

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Pages | `src/pages/` | Route screens; keep thin |
| Components | `src/components/` | Composed UI |
| Hooks | `src/hooks/` | State and flow logic |
| Services | `src/services/` | API calls via `apiClient` |
| Shared | `src/shared/` | Reusable UI, avatar helpers, storage |

## Rules

- TypeScript **strict** — avoid `any`
- User-visible text via **i18n keys** in `src/locales/` — not hardcoded strings
- API calls only through `src/services/` — not inline `fetch` in components
- Game outcomes and simulation rules come from the **backend** — frontend displays results

## Build and lint

```bash
cd frontend && npm run build   # tsc + vite build
make lint-frontend             # ESLint
make format-check-frontend     # Prettier check
make format-frontend           # Prettier write
```

Do not replace `vite.config.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, or Tailwind scaffolding by hand — see `no-framework-scaffolding.mdc`.
